      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r1iOzVzMPBCn-WNs_Co6d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 957.3153181506221,
      "y": 726.8792703290334,
      "width": 1326.6000000000001,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1080170512,
      "version": 902,
      "versionNonce": 1730887408,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1792936779055,
      "created": 1792934596007,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive 1: how to scale to support 1B users?\n- estimate: 1B users, ~20% online -> 200M concurrent ws; 100K~1M conn/host -> 200~2000 Realtime hosts; 100B msg/day -> ~1M\nmsg/s\n- Chat Realtime Service from single host to cluster\n- How to route msg between cluster? -> Redis pub/sub, Kafka, consistent hash\n    - Kafka: topic per user impossible, consumer group rebalance slow (built for throughput, not ms-level point-to-point push)\n    - consistent hash: unstable when changing, hard to maintain (need registry + direct RPC between hosts)\n    - Redis pub/sub: cheap and quick (at most once, but could be covered by Message/Inbox)\n        - channel per userId (clientId), subscribe on connect, unsubscribe on disconnect\n        - ~1M publish/s -> Redis Cluster sharded pub/sub, shard by userId\n        - online user misses a dropped publish -> host sweeps Inbox for its connected users every ~30s (or heartbeat carries last seq)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive 1: how to scale to support 1B users?\n- estimate: 1B users, ~20% online -> 200M concurrent ws; 100K~1M conn/host -> 200~2000 Realtime hosts; 100B msg/day -> ~1M msg/s\n- Chat Realtime Service from single host to cluster\n- How to route msg between cluster? -> Redis pub/sub, Kafka, consistent hash\n    - Kafka: topic per user impossible, consumer group rebalance slow (built for throughput, not ms-level point-to-point push)\n    - consistent hash: unstable when changing, hard to maintain (need registry + direct RPC between hosts)\n    - Redis pub/sub: cheap and quick (at most once, but could be covered by Message/Inbox)\n        - channel per userId (clientId), subscribe on connect, unsubscribe on disconnect\n        - ~1M publish/s -> Redis Cluster sharded pub/sub, shard by userId\n        - online user misses a dropped publish -> host sweeps Inbox for its connected users every ~30s (or heartbeat carries last seq)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
